pkg:Evidence_v1_38_0 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.38.0 (real WSJF prioritisation: STORY-8 selected over STORY-10)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "MINOR: ran the framework's own real WSJF method (backlog:Method_WSJF, the canonical individual used across the framework's own fixtures) to choose between STORY-8 and STORY-10 rather than an ad-hoc pick. STORY-8 scored 2.5, STORY-10 scored 1.0 -- driven by STORY-10's own disclosed structural blocker (cannot be behaviourally tested in this environment, no live LLM), which raises its effective job size past what its value justifies now. Confirmed via the framework's own --next selection independently, which chose STORY-8 on its own. Found STORY-8 was not yet genuinely Ready by the framework's real definition (a real AcceptanceCriterion was missing); groomed it properly -- wrote a real, testable Gherkin AC, added the real design concerns its scope touches, and a RefinementEvent recording the actual grooming performed. Re-verified: pipeline order PASS, register back to CONFORMANT after grooming, --next re-confirms STORY-8."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "505064299435553777be09685cbb153752bc9ea24f28beb916035257cb0d6397"^^xsd:string .
